    "expectedRule": "Chapter 5 records the opening style of every non-boss fight: the first attack, art or guard action decides force, art or guard. Over the won fights in order, two consecutive wins with the same style make it a repeat that costs that style -20% (force/art outgoing damage or guard effect); once all three styles have won at least once the ruling is rewritten to +10% force, +10% art and +10% guard effect, which overrides any repeat. Display: title 熔炉判词; status `已记录 n/3` (stable), `连续复招：力|术|守` (danger) or `三式齐全，裁决改判` (resolved); meter {styles seen, 3}; targetReached only when rewritten. An art costs 1 focus and fights start at 0 focus, so the art opening first spends the gate_sense method technique (rank 1: +1 focus, not a combat action) and then casts. Gates: arena_force_champion_lane, arena_art_bench_lane and arena_guard_oath_lane open after one win with force, art or guard; arena_three_style_judge_lane opens once all three styles have won. A closed style lane reads `先用力|术|守式开局获胜 1 场。`. The pursuer is a separate run system and is disabled after entry so it cannot ambush the walk. The hero is raised to body 18 (AC-LAW-CORE-05 used body 10) so that plain attacks still win all four arena fights against the monsters refitted to the standard player curve; body only changes HP, attack, defense and resistance, and no expected value below depends on it. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
